      "title": "Troubleshooting Autoscaling Failures in Secret Store",
      "content_summary": "Addresses scenarios where Secret Store autoscaling fails to trigger, often manifesting as rate limit errors or suspected memory leaks. This guide focuses on identifying resource exhaustion and misconfigured rate limits.",
      "content_body": "When autoscaling fails to trigger for Secret Store, check if the service is hitting hard rate limits before scaling policies activate. Verify that the memory usage metrics are not being skewed by transient spikes or agent-side memory leaks. Ensure your autoscaling policy thresholds align with the actual traffic patterns rather than default conservative settings. If rate limit misconfiguration is confirmed, adjust the API gateway limits to allow for burst traffic during scale-out events. Finally, request a capacity increase if the underlying infrastructure is consistently showing resource exhaustion despite correct scaling configurations."
